#: ../../libraries/drives.rst:2 154bfdbdbad24aa787d48b33bf51bb97
msgid "Adding and removing drives"
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/drives.rst:4 3bb9993edc3f4a7aaa23ac3cb615161a
msgid ""
"A library's drives are part of its configuration, so adding or removing "
"one rewrites ``device.conf`` and restarts the library."
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/drives.rst:12 1eade526c44b466ca489b599b6e345e5
msgid "Adding a drive"
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/drives.rst:14 4c20d13339d74000add05c46c21fe964
msgid ""
"**Operator → Add Drive**, or **Drives → Add a drive** on the library "
"page, which arrives with the library already chosen."
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/drives.rst:17 773d438e59374e1eaadf6662052908be
msgid ""
"The page shows what the drive will be before you commit to it: the model,"
" the serial it will be given, the slot it will occupy, and its SCSI "
"address. Change the library and all of that changes with it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/drives.rst:21 37ee9389202b43cd9ddfa08df3d622fb
msgid ""
"Only drives this library's model takes are offered - plus any model the "
"library already holds, because a library on a real host does not always "
"match its profile, and refusing a drive identical to the ones already in "
"it would help nobody."
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/drives.rst:26 70c96286e9e049bc9386cc4d3c535006
msgid "Add Drive: the models this library takes, and where the drive will go"
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/drives.rst:39 23d250dc23be4f0eb934f179453a1b3d
msgid ""
"The slot, the drive id and the SCSI target are chosen for you: they are "
"the next free ones. Overriding them is not offered, because a drive at an"
" address something else already uses will not start."
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/drives.rst:44 58ef7fd6bc7b4c418f89c6e6fdc46f48
msgid "Removing a drive"
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/drives.rst:46 840da181b7b8444d8f846d3592e25811
msgid ""
"**Operator → Remove Drive**, or **Drives → Remove a drive** on the "
"library page."
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/drives.rst:49 382fb63b2fa84283b05839b6aa077827
msgid ""
"The page says what is in the drive before you remove it. A drive holding "
"a tape has that tape put back in its slot first."
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/drives.rst:52 21e4f0d631c9408c8175605082b67bb4
msgid "Remove Drive: which drive, and what it is holding"
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/drives.rst:63 108dc6bba06340b1b491f9ec61cd50e8
msgid ""
"This cannot be undone, although the drive can be added again. What it "
"removes is the drive's entry in ``device.conf``; no tape is deleted."
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/drives.rst:67 08168b948ff14aa696b293460e6becf4
msgid "What it does to the running library"
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/drives.rst:69 a3ae89a1166b42389655cc3c90f7f7a0
msgid ""
"Both restart the library, because MHVTL reads ``device.conf`` once, when "
"a daemon starts. Until it restarts, its robot reports the drives it had "
"when it started."
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/drives.rst:73 5828add482144e94a38fcf6641a66fcc
msgid ""
"``--no-restart`` writes the configuration and leaves the daemons alone, "
"for when you are making several changes and want one restart at the end:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/drives.rst:82 fb3299822ae541a4aa5ed0f40f982aea
msgid ""
"The console says the same thing, on the page: a library whose "
"configuration and whose robot disagree is flagged until it is restarted."
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/drives.rst:86 db9e2c73d7b94d5db380f158a0b7468e
msgid "Seeing the drives"
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/drives.rst:98 b0a2e1cad755498789cfc65cb1666cb8
msgid "Two generations in one library"
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/drives.rst:100 5dde3a20cfd34d0d93aedb51a9036fd7
msgid ""
"A library does not have to hold one kind of drive. A real site that has "
"just bought LTO-9 drives still has shelves of LTO-7 cartridges, and the "
"library that can read the old tapes and write the new ones is one library"
" with both kinds of drive in it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/drives.rst:105 3bdbbe4c06e04f3a9b5e0fc5ab022704
msgid "The console builds that in one step, and so does the command line."
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/drives.rst:108 84cdcd0bbaa142aa8bdcb418f67c8534
msgid "In the console"
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/drives.rst:110 cc017cfbbb0c4a62b102d037e8ae2d91
msgid ""
"On the library form, **Add another drive type** adds a second row: a "
"model and a count. **Add another cartridge type** does the same for the "
"media. The limits still come from the library model, so only drives that "
"model takes are offered in either row."
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/drives.rst:115 619ccd792dce44afb172d43a3af65b57
msgid ""
"The rows are in slot order, which is also SCSI target order - so the "
"first row is the first drive. A backup application that addresses a drive"
" by its position notices if that order changes, which is why the order "
"you enter is the order that is written."
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/drives.rst:121 355a3784ff09494e8291f4b6385f0edf
msgid "From the terminal"
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/drives.rst:123 b0e41232c28e4d00a05903195cef401c
msgid "``--drive`` and ``--media`` repeat, each naming a model and how many:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/drives.rst:131 e052beb2bd444fc6bb3f009a962b0ef1
msgid ""
"Two LTO-10 drives, two LTO-9 drives, twenty LTO-10 cartridges and ten "
"LTO-9 ones. Barcodes follow the runs in order: the first twenty end "
"``LA``, the next ten end ``L9``, and the numbering runs straight through "
"the two."
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/drives.rst:135 ac7fe2695c8d43389ae73f774e2a5e9a
msgid ""
"``--drive`` replaces ``--drives`` and ``--media`` replaces ``--tapes``, "
"and naming both of a pair is refused - a count and a list are two answers"
" to one question, and nothing can choose between them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/drives.rst:139 cd0e6d0f945447edb97fb140b763f2ca
msgid ""
"``mhvtl library create --interactive`` asks the same thing as **Add "
"another drive type?**; see :doc:`create-interactively`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/drives.rst:143 f68cd223b5ff45c38e832a393630a2ac
msgid "What a mixed library can load"
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/drives.rst:145 ecd305508ae04bed8a4c4a6aa0b52934
msgid ""
"``mhvtl tape media`` is the one command to ask, because the answer is the"
" union of what all the drives do, and it is not obvious by inspection:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/drives.rst:162 9067a630363d42ae82001e0857aeab90
msgid ""
"Five generations in a library with two kinds of drive, and the **USE** "
"column is the part to read. LTO4 is ``read-only``: that cartridge can be "
"loaded and read, and the library will refuse to make a new one, because "
"an LTO-6 drive reads LTO-4 but cannot write it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/drives.rst:167 f79d64b4d9ff44aab41972cafb152b49
msgid ""
"The same table is what the tape form offers, so a cartridge the console "
"lets you create is one the library can really write."
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/drives.rst:171 268ac9bcd9d34fb2bc98427776cd4b4b
msgid "Adding a generation later"
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/drives.rst:173 a4732a815f8f4facbf9f555ac8ec647a
msgid ""
"A library does not have to be built mixed. ``drive add`` takes ``--drive-"
"model``, so the second generation can arrive the way it does in real life"
" - bought later and racked beside the first:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/drives.rst:181 0017e462fd524b29a0f4f0845ae116cf
msgid ""
"The new drive widens what the library can load, and ``tape media`` says "
"so immediately. Nothing about the existing drives or cartridges changes."
msgstr ""

